== CCX vs STANDARD FaIR, matched: 100 GtC in 2050 on ssp245, FaIR 2.2.4 calib 1.6.0, 841 configs ==
       yr |   AF ccx  AF fair   ratio | K/1000 ccx     fair   ratio
     2080 |   0.5088   0.5468   0.931 |      1.339    1.366   0.981
     2150 |   0.3141   0.4687   0.670 |      1.082    1.390   0.779
     2230 |   0.2539   0.4376   0.580 |      1.025    1.447   0.709
     2300 |   0.2249   0.4130   0.545 |      1.005    1.489   0.675
   ⭐ READ THE TWO RATIO COLUMNS TOGETHER. If they track each other, the
     temperature difference IS the airborne-fraction difference and the
     climate half (shared with FaIR by construction) is exonerated.
   ⚠ FaIR's per-1000 RISES with horizon while CCX's FALLS -- so the gap is
     not a constant offset and quoting it at one horizon understates it.
   ⚠ The FaIR arm is on RCMIP-native ssp245 emissions, not the CMIP7-
     harmonised set the 1.6.0 posterior was jointly conditioned on. That is
     what the CCX module itself was built from, so it is the matched choice
     here; it is expected to largely cancel in a MARGINAL and was not measured.
   ⚠ FaIR's per-config marginal is right-skewed: median(pulse-base) runs ~5 %
     BELOW the mean. CCX has one ensemble-MEAN module, so the mean is the
     matched statistic -- but the median would narrow this gap, not widen it.

